    "summary": "Electric Dark Star & The Other One dominate first European gig",
    "blurb": "The band delivers a high‑energy set highlighted by a soaring Dark Star and a punchy Hard To Handle. Jerry’s lead work is front‑and‑center while Pigpen’s organ shines on Lovelight. Overall the show captures historic momentum despite some mix quirks.",
    "review": "On May 24, 1970, the Grateful Dead made their first European appearance at Newcastle‑Under‑Lyme, and the performance lives up to its historic status. The set opens with a rollicking Casey Jones before diving into a blistering Dark Star that many reviewers describe as “breathtaking” and “electric,” showcasing Garcia’s soaring lead work. The Other One follows with fluid transitions, and Hard To Handle erupts with extra burst of energy. Pigpen takes the helm on Turn On Your Lovelight, while the rhythm section—Bob’s steady guitar, Phil’s bass (thin early but solid later), and Bill’s massive drumming—keeps the momentum driving forward. Standout moments include Me And My Uncle, Attics Of My Life, Good Lovin’ (double‑cut), and a heartfelt Cold Rain And Snow, all wrapped up in a historic festival atmosphere despite occasional tape hiss and level peaking on some matrix sources.",
